<section class="container page-intro narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Quality & documentation</p><h1>Ask for evidence.<br> Know what it covers.</h1><p class="lead">Quality documentation is most useful when it relates to your instrument, your supplier and your destination market.</p><a class="button" href="/request-quote?intent=documentation">Request documentation ↗</a></section>
<section class="section soft"><div class="container editorial-columns"><div><h2>Start with the product reference.</h2><p>Send the references you are evaluating and the country in which you intend to supply them. Specify the documents your procurement or regulatory team needs to review.</p><p>Current certificates and product-specific compliance documents are not published on this website. Request the applicable documents and verify their issuer, scope and validity before an order.</p><a class="text-link" href="/products">Find an instrument reference ↗</a></div><div class="checklist"><h3>Include in your documentation request</h3><ul><li>Product names and catalogue references</li><li>Destination country and intended sourcing requirements</li><li>Required material and dimensional specifications</li><li>Applicable certificates and declarations</li><li>Instructions for use and reprocessing information, where relevant</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section class="section container"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Different documents. Different meanings.</h2></div><div class="service-rows"><div><h3>ISO 13485 certification</h3><p>Relates to a medical-device quality management system within a stated scope. Review the certificate holder, scope, issuing body and validity; it is not product approval.</p></div><div><h3>FDA establishment registration</h3><p>Establishment registration and device listing do not mean FDA approval. Product-specific requirements must be considered separately.</p></div><div><h3>CE marking</h3><p>Applies to a product under relevant European requirements. Ask for the applicable declaration and supporting documents; a CE graphic alone is not evidence of conformity.</p></div></div><p class="small-note">These descriptions explain document types. They do not claim that Surgical Essence or any listed product holds a certification, registration or authorisation.</p><p class="small-note">Further guidance: <a href="https://www.iso.org/iso-13485-medical-devices.html">ISO 13485</a>, <a href="https://www.fda.gov/medical-devices/device-registration-and-listing/important-reminders-about-registration-and-listing">FDA registration and listing</a>, and <a href="https://health.ec.europa.eu/medical-devices-sector/overview_en">European Commission medical-device guidance</a>.</p></section><%- include('partials/cta') %>
